    82	### 1.2 Lemma A (every component is a polynomial curve) `[D]`
    83	
    84	> **Lemma A.** Let `D` be any component of `A_F` and `l` any affine-image
    85	> dicritical with image `D`. Then `D~ ≃ A^1`, `D` has exactly one place at
    86	> infinity, and `h_l : A^1 → A^1` is a degree-`s_l` polynomial map whose finite
    87	> ramification satisfies `Σ_t (e_t − 1) = s_l − 1`.
    88	
    89	*Proof.* By (G6), `l' ≃ A^1`; by (G3), `h_l : A^1 → D~` is finite surjective of
    90	degree `s := s_l`. Let `D~^c` be the smooth projective model of `D~`, of genus
    91	`g`, and `B = D~^c \ D~` its (nonempty, since `D~` is affine) set of places at
    92	infinity. Extend to `h^c : P^1 → D~^c`, still of degree `s` and surjective. No
    93	finite point of `A^1` maps into `B`, because `h_l(A^1) ⊆ D~`; and every point of
    94	`B` has a preimage. Hence `B = {h^c(∞)}` is a single place and `∞` is its only
    95	preimage, so `e_∞ = s`. Riemann–Hurwitz gives
    96	`−2 = s(2g − 2) + (s − 1) + R_fin` with `R_fin = Σ_{finite}(e_t − 1) ≥ 0`. If
    97	`g ≥ 1` the right side is `≥ 0`; hence `g = 0`, and then `R_fin = s − 1`. So
    98	`D~^c ≃ P^1`, `|B| = 1`, `D~ ≃ A^1`. ∎
